projections, held to regeneration
  graph_export exports/control.json
    not committed, and this run would write it
  graph_export exports/filtered.json
    not committed, and this run would write it
  site_nav .headwater/nav.yml
    not committed, and this run would write it
  corpus_descriptor .headwater/corpus.json
    not committed, and this run would write it

what this verb does not write, and why
  shelf_index shelf `answers`
    no `shelf_index` declaration names the shelf `answers`, so no index is written for it. To add one, name `answers` in the `for` of a `shelf_index` declaration, or declare `{kind: shelf_index, for: [answers], output: "{shelf}/README.md"}` under `add_to: projections:` in `.headwater/overlay.yml`
  template no declaration names one
    a template is the permitted relations, facets and sections of a kind, which `headwater explain` already prints. What no document states is the file it goes in
  transcription no declaration names one
    a transcription needs a resolver that reads text from a pinned snapshot, and Q19 leaves whether it ships at all to the first adopter who asks
  coverage_report the register
    its content is a function of the clock as well as of the corpus and the lock, because a migration task lapses and a suppression expires on a date. A committed copy would fail this check on a morning when nothing changed. The register of open obligations carries it
